From 30ef85738180c2fdc41676f1650ff5a4ccd39120 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 11:37:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 115/115] bcm2835-sdiod: the Pi Zero 2 W (CYW43436 family) next
 to the Pi 3B+

Board from the devicetree. On the Zero 2 W WL_REG_ON is GPIO 41 and the
chip gets its 32.768 kHz sleep clock from GPCLK2 on GPIO 43. Chips with an
ARM CM3 and SOCRAM (CYW43430/43436) download and start as in brcmfmac.
Firmware and NVRAM by chip ID and revision as Raspberry Pi OS does,
fw=<name> overrides; the CLM file is optional for those chips. The driver
asks the firmware whether it has its own supplicant (sup_wpa). wlan0
reports its link state (up after the join, then from link events).
